+//
+// Returns the index in `v` of the sample that owns (ring, station, stationChan),
+// or -1 with *why set to a short code:
+//   "bad-address"      ring < 0, station <= 0 or stationChan < 0 was ASKED for
+//   "not-in-card-map"  no ring-attributed sample carries that address
+//
+// ⚠ Differs from the display rule on purpose. ResolveIoPoint accepts a flat
+//   sample (ring == -1) because a lamp can afford to be wrong about the ring;
+//   a write cannot. Two reasons, both recorded against this tree:
+//     * station 1 is a SERVOPACK on ring 0 and a 32DO on ring 1 (card map
