+//   -- exactly the condition under which Execute takes the Ex path.
+// ⚠ It does not look at `valid`. Whether a byte that did not read back may be
+//   written or trusted is the caller's decision, and the route refuses both.
+// First match wins, the same as ResolveIoPoint, so the lamp and the write can
+// never pick two different bytes for one address.
+int PickIoSample(const std::vector<IoByteSample>& v, int ring, int station, int stationChan,
+                 const char** why);
